{"parentUuid":"6ff95ab9-e608-4126-a4d3-985882706a2e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Ganr5PpL2Z3B1krAK7efyH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to know if I can read .seospider format files from Screaming Frog. Let me look at what the Screaming Frog MCP tools can do more carefully.\n\nThe tools available are:\n- `crawl_site` - start a new crawl\n- `crawl_status` - check crawl status\n- `delete_crawl` - delete a crawl\n- `export_crawl` - export a crawl\n- `list_crawls` - list crawls saved in Screaming Frog's internal database\n- `read_crawl_data` - read CSV data from an export\n- `sf_check` - check something\n\n\n- `storage_summary` - storage summary\n\nThe `list_crawls` tool retrieves crawls from Screaming Frog's internal database, but a `.seospider` file is the proprietary format for saved crawls. The MCP likely interfaces with a running Screaming Frog instance, so opening a `.seospider` file in the application would make it accessible through these tools. Let me explore the available tool schemas to understand the full capabilities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":827,"cache_read_input_tokens":17971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":827},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CZCS7Mnpv5EDU46g7d4Wj","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0150138-0a38-4ff9-aa25-dc52ba47e335","timestamp":"2026-03-19T12:24:36.810Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/a39326","sessionId":"b7fe4655-d467-4510-b706-83bb0fa914f6","version":"2.1.79","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
