{"parentUuid":"7132b9d6-86a3-4f23-bffc-2276d41961c6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01UkLCrvihduw1eaB4DfTnnJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a better picture of the Screaming Frog MCP tools. Let me explain what's possible with .seospider files.\n\nThe Screaming Frog MCP works with Screaming Frog's **internal database** (crawls stored in SF's own storage), not directly with `.seospider` files on disk. \n\nHowever, `.seospider` files can be opened/loaded into Screaming Frog SEO Spider, and then they'd appear in the internal database that `list_crawls` can access.\n\nThe workflow would be:\n1. Open the `.seospider` file in Screaming Frog SEO Spider desktop app\n\n\n2. Once it's in the internal database, I can use `list_crawls` to find it, then `export_crawl` with the db_id to export it as CSV, and finally `read_crawl_data` to access the data.\n\nSo the answer is: not directly from the file path, but if the file is loaded into Screaming Frog's internal database, yes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":18798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1024},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CZCS7zujkV93drB2zdmGp","type":"assistant","uuid":"021a2bda-72ab-4082-ad78-21b013a4743d","timestamp":"2026-03-19T12:24:44.213Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/a39326","sessionId":"b7fe4655-d467-4510-b706-83bb0fa914f6","version":"2.1.79","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"021a2bda-72ab-4082-ad78-21b013a4743d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01UkLCrvihduw1eaB4DfTnnJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Screaming Frog MCP tools **cannot read a `.seospider` file directly by path**. They work with crawls stored in Screaming Frog's **internal database**.\n\nHowever, you can access your `.seospider` file in two steps:\n\n**Step 1 — Load it into Screaming Frog's database:**\nOpen the `.seospider` file in the Screaming Frog SEO Spider desktop app, then save it via *File → Save As* to SF's internal storage.\n\n**Step 2 — Access it via MCP:**\nOnce saved internally, the workflow is:\n1. `list_crawls` → find your crawl's Database ID\n2. `export_crawl` (with the `db_id`) → exports data as CSV files\n3. `read_crawl_data` → read the CSV data\n\nWant me to run `list_crawls` now to see what's already in Screaming Frog's database?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":18798,"output_tokens":483,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1024,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CZCS7zujkV93drB2zdmGp","type":"assistant","uuid":"ffc0c9ea-a380-458c-b1cd-77b8f55bbcc3","timestamp":"2026-03-19T12:24:46.651Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/a39326","sessionId":"b7fe4655-d467-4510-b706-83bb0fa914f6","version":"2.1.79","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
